# repos

`mise run clone` clones the {{ project_name }} repositories here. The folder is in `.gitignore`; only this file is tracked.

Each clone has its own `.git`, branches, git hooks and agent rules. Clone changes are committed to their own repositories, following each clone's branch model ([docs/agents/branches.md](../docs/agents/branches.md)).

## Which repositories are cloned

`repos.toml` in the root is the list. `mise run add-repo` adds a repository; `mise run repos:sync` regenerates from it `[bootstrap.repos]` in `mise.toml`, which `mise run clone` reads, the sdd-kit list `openspec/clones` and the table below.

<!-- repos:begin -->

No repositories yet. Add one with `mise run add-repo`.

<!-- repos:end -->

## How it works

`mise run clone` reads `[bootstrap.repos]` and runs `git clone` for each missing clone, on its rest branch. Existing clones are left as they are, on their branch and with their changes. `mise run pull` runs `git pull --rebase --autostash` in each clone on its current branch and at the end lists the clones that could not be updated.

Private repositories are usually cloned over SSH, so you need an SSH key with access to each repository in the list.

A clone folder must not exist before the first clone, because `git clone` does not write into a non-empty folder. That is why only this README is here.

## What is not allowed here

Do not create files in `repos/` by hand; all content comes from cloning. Do not clone repositories bypassing `repos.toml`, otherwise they are left out of the tasks and checks.
